# Single-focus scheduling

**Core principle:** A user can only do one task at a time. **Two task blocks must never overlap** on the timeline.

## Engine (`packages/core`)

- `SINGLE_FOCUS_TASK_SCHEDULING` invariant in `timeline-scheduling.ts`
- Use `buildTimelineInsertPushBackUpdates` before placing a task — never set `scheduledAt` alone without push-back
- `findOverlappingCalendarEvents` for static GCal blocks (exception path)

## Calendar exception (N-0020 + N-0021)

- Google Calendar events may overlap tasks (reference / shared calendar)
- Show `ScheduleConflictDialog` before committing; user may confirm
- Render overlapping task + event in **side-by-side columns** via `computeTimelineOverlapLayout`

## All schedule paths must use

- `useTimelineSchedule` / `checkCalendarConflictsForNewTask` for calendar gate
- `applyTimelinePushBackForInsert` or `addToTimeline` for task push-back
